note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note omegese-om2.md 2 line 54: a hex literal takes the type the place needs: array length, fill
note value, index, put value, for count, call argument, comparison operand, operand of sub, fd and
note offset of write. Expected stdout/exit: oracle/s0s2/oracle.py (hex_places). Used with lib/putu.om.
om2
text msg "hex\n"
fn twice a ulong to ulong
ret mul a 2
end
fn main to int
a = new uchar 0x4 0x0
put a 0x1 0x68
put a 0x3 0xa
s = ulong 0x0
for i ulong 0x5
s = add s i
end
putu s
putu twice 0x15
putu ulong get a 0x1
if eq s 0xa
putu 0xabc
end
x = int 0x10
y = sub x 0x20
if lt y 0x0
putu ulong neg y
end
r = write 0x1 msg 0x0 len msg
ret int get a 0x3
end
